+# N03 normal-owner complete observed-anchor → native route → collision connection
+
+Source-only third-layer proposal based on the reviewed NEXT40 source inputs. No Apple build, native fixture or device capture has run for this patch. The exact five-file core checkpoint is recorded alongside this note;41 bounded source contracts passed. These are source checks, not Swift execution or measured navigation accuracy. Integration of the separate strict26 Apple companion remains pending.
+
+## Actual source connection
+
+The existing opt-in `DEBUG && BLIND_MESH_CANDIDATE_DIAGNOSTICS` owner no longer merely counts and refuses updates. The normal ARSession/delegate stays in place. After urgent depth/hazard processing, a fresh tracked frame supplies its complete **observed anchor inventory**, bounded at 128 inspected AR anchors / 32 mesh identities including tombstones. Native buffers remain on the serialized owning callback. At most one whole anchor is copied per admitted frame using the existing `ARKitMeshAdapter82` / decoder81 checks and `MeshCandidateIngress83`; neither the 512-face history sampler nor an LLM supplies this geometry.
+
+New/changed/resized/omitted anchors retire output and enter the existing unresolved-delivery ledger. Actual removals remain distinct from missing observations. Dirty stable anchors are retried with a rotating one-copy selection; no omitted anchor is erased to make delivery complete. This does **not** weaken83's global-gap contract or create observed-world completeness. Missing/malformed classifications remain unknown; `.classifiedFloorOnly` does not make them walkable.
+
+An explicit developer action freezes the actual current LocalPlanner's two look-ahead endpoints and the declared body/profile/mount. A real75 strict-XZ query proposes a **new Detour route between those endpoints**, not a certification of the LocalPlanner's intermediate polyline. Exact post-query original83 source, all original Y values, mixed floor/obstacle/unknown roles, and the existing shared `SeatedMeshRouteAudit` provide raw-body and separate-margin initial/sweep/terminal checks, including requested/projected/native connectors. Geometry is not reconstructed from a pretty picture or moved to make the path pass.
+
+The look-ahead start is not the wearer foot. No camera-to-start connector, body localization, floor support, contained start, solid volume, stairs completeness or physical clearance is invented. No-contact remains unknown. The UI displays historical native coordinates plus requested/native endpoint associations, never normal walking speech. The source is from the same sensor; the collision algorithm is independent, the observation is not.
+
+## Explicit limits and ownership
+
+- 32 retained mesh IDs/tombstones, 30,000 total vertices and 30,000 total triangles, including retained missing-anchor sizes; whole-anchor refusal, not truncation. These are **our implementation admission limits**, not room impassability or iPhone inability.
+- One owned82 copy/decode slot; 1.5MB per-copy input/decoded ceilings and 2MB source snapshot payload limit. Native/SceneKit derived allocation and capture latency are not measured by these ceilings.
+- <=0.5s tracked frame and depth-plan admission; an explicitly frozen request remains historical for at most8s while a current tracked same-session lease remains available. Ordinary later frames do not silently substitute pose/endpoints. Geometry revision, goal, profile, mount, tracking/session, malformed replacement, stop and expiry retire it.
+- Companion goal String and local intent UUID remain separate namespaces, both checked. Read-time UI getters are pure, not `objectWillChange` producers.
+- One source/query/audit operation at a time, native serial domain unchanged. Original raw source is cleared after scoped audit return before a main-queue drain barrier. Terminal ownership acknowledgement waits actual native discard **and** source/query/collider operation return. Native/SceneKit synchronous calls are not forcibly preemptible; existing audit checks its cooperative5s budget between calls.
+- Full observed surfaces still do not supply a fresh full-footprint floor-support producer. Unobserved remote geometry versus swept-route support should be evaluated separately in future work, but this patch does not relax existing83 global refusal to guess that distinction.
+
+## Authored native fixtures (unrun)
+
+`NormalOwnerMeshConnectionTests` has five explicitly named cases: incomplete/bounded inventory; reordered/future/session/expiry rejection; real mixed-role owned82→83→75→collider result retaining a frozen request across an ordinary frame and rejecting later malformed replacement; a32-anchor one-copy/15Hz sequence retaining >1.9s-old receipt history while the latest frame lease advances; and held **real** oracle progress with goal/source/stop retirement and terminal-discard withholding until the actual audit is released. All waits remain10s, standalone cleanup expectations have one teardown waiter, and successive owners drain before allocation of the next fixture owner. No ARFrame, validated snapshot, native result or successful collision receipt is fabricated.
+
+Native membership/selection/strict26 collector wiring and explicit existing81/82 app product links are a separate pending CI companion after core review; this packet is not yet an executable Apple adoption checkpoint. Source-only controls do not prove Swift compilation or accuracy.
+
+## Reuse provenance
+
+Unchanged in this patch: pinned project adapters81/82/83 and75 (Recast/Detour), their ownership/decoder guards, strict endpoint policy and classified-floor-only mode; existing shared Apple SceneKit cylinder/contact oracle and controls through `SeatedMeshRouteAudit`. Existing repository adoption/provenance and license records remain controlling. No new package, detector, mapper, permission, network upload or calibration is introduced.
+
+The 32-anchor cadence fixture uses actual owned82 buffers and83 source snapshots. It asserts complete observed delivery after more than2s while surface capture timestamps remain unavailable. It does not call historical receipt age current surface observation age. The new visible result explicitly reports oldest receipt age and unavailable capture age; ongoing tracked frames do not renew old surface evidence into movement support.
+
+## Camera-owner handoff
+
+A stopped or disabled full-mesh owner may still retain native/source/audit work. Existing exclusive seated-bench and RoomPlan starts now refuse *before* camera transfer while that ownership exists. The explicit release action waits the actual combined discard acknowledgement; it neither starts nor stops the normal camera/hazard loop. Initially unused owners pass; terminally released owners pass only after drain, and require app relaunch for another full-mesh diagnostic. The seated confirmation remains single-use, so release requires re-confirmation rather than an automatic delayed handoff. The held-oracle fixture asserts native ACK alone still cannot yield camera ownership. Same-ID removed anchors that reappear require a new owned copy/revision; tombstones are retained, not mistaken for installed geometry.
+
+**Latency warning:** the visible control warning requires seated developer testing. Full-buffer copying and the reused synchronous MainActor SceneKit collision calls may delay later camera alerts; checking this frame's urgent hazards first does not guarantee subsequent hazard latency. Normal camera ownership is retained, not a promise of uninterrupted hazard processing. No unreviewed background collision implementation or scheduling change is introduced; native/phone latency remains unmeasured.
